Fixed. Both tests (4) and typecheck pass.

**The bug:** `src/sim.ts:43` — `if (foodSurplus >= 0)` grew population whenever food production met or exceeded consumption. A settlement producing exactly as much food as it consumes has a surplus of 0, which satisfied `>= 0`, so population grew turn after turn even at break-even.

**The fix:** changed `>= 0` to `> 0`, so population grows only on an actual surplus (production strictly greater than consumption).


